<section class="ck-hero"><div class="ck-w ck-hero-g"><div><p class="ck-tag">// set &middot; use &middot; maintain</p><h1>Know your watch.<br><span>Down to the second.</span></h1><p class="ck-lead">Clocked is an independent guide to living with a watch. We explain how to set it safely, how to use a second time zone and how to keep it running well for years.</p><p class="ck-acts"><a class="btn" href="#tools">Open the tools</a><a class="ck-ln" href="watch-setting-guide.html">How to set a watch &rarr;</a></p><div class="ck-stats"><div><b>9 pm&ndash;3 am</b><span>date-change danger zone</span></div><div><b>24 h</b><span>GMT hand rotation</span></div><div><b>40&ndash;80 h</b><span>typical power reserve</span></div></div></div><figure class="ck-hero-f"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1793917943279-31be5cf1fe47?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=620&q=75" alt="silver wristwatch with a blue dial and exposed movement" width="560" height="620" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>EXPOSED MOVEMENT &middot; BLUE DIAL</figcaption></figure></div></section>

<section class="ck-s"><div class="ck-w"><div class="ck-st"><span>01</span><h2>Three things every watch owner should know</h2></div><div class="ck-cards">
<article><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1793059669214-450230eadfe4?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=280&q=75" alt="man in a black blazer checking his watch" width="420" height="280" loading="lazy"><div><h3>Set it forwards</h3><p>Move the hands clockwise and keep away from the date change zone when using quick-set.</p></div></article>
<article><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1792683422265-47b5f7c2afd5?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=280&q=75" alt="two-tone wristwatch on a wooden stand" width="420" height="280" loading="lazy"><div><h3>Keep it running</h3><p>An automatic needs wrist time or a few turns of the crown. Know your power reserve.</p></div></article>
<article><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1793508025176-0c36412a76e9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=280&q=75" alt="tattooed hand wearing a metal watch" width="420" height="280" loading="lazy"><div><h3>Respect the crown</h3><p>Push it in or screw it down before water. An open crown is the most common cause of moisture inside.</p></div></article></div></div></section>

<section class="ck-tl" id="tools"><div class="ck-w"><div class="ck-st ck-st-d"><span>02</span><h2>Watch tools</h2></div><div class="ck-panel">
<div class="ck-mod"><h3>Safe Date Setter</h3><p class="ck-md">Can you use the quick-set date right now?</p><label for="sd-t">Time shown on the watch<input id="sd-t" type="time" value="22:15"></label><label for="sd-ap">Watch type<select id="sd-ap"><option value="mech">Mechanical with date</option><option value="quartz">Quartz with date</option></select></label><div class="ck-lcd" id="sd-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div>
<div class="ck-mod"><h3>GMT Bezel Planner</h3><p class="ck-md">Set the bezel for a second time zone.</p><label for="gm-h">Home time zone (UTC offset)<select id="gm-h"></select></label><label for="gm-a">Second time zone (UTC offset)<select id="gm-a"></select></label><div class="ck-lcd" id="gm-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div>
<div class="ck-mod"><h3>Power Reserve Tracker</h3><p class="ck-md">Will it still be running when you pick it up?</p><label for="pr-r">Power reserve (hours)<input id="pr-r" type="number" min="20" max="240" step="2" value="42"></label><label for="pr-o">Hours off the wrist<input id="pr-o" type="number" min="0" max="400" step="1" value="30"></label><div class="ck-lcd" id="pr-out" aria-live="polite"></div></div>
</div></div></section>

<section class="ck-s"><div class="ck-w ck-zone"><div><div class="ck-st"><span>03</span><h2>The date change danger zone</h2></div><p class="ck-lead">On most mechanical date watches, the date wheel starts to engage a few hours before midnight. Forcing the quick-set while it is engaged can damage the mechanism.</p><ol class="ck-steps"><li>Pull the crown to the time-setting position.</li><li>Move the hands to about 6:00 (well clear of midnight).</li><li>Push to the date position and set the date to yesterday.</li><li>Pull back out and wind the hands forwards past midnight to today.</li><li>Set the correct time, then push or screw the crown fully home.</li></ol></div><div class="ck-dial" aria-hidden="true"><div class="ck-dz"></div><div class="ck-dc"><b>DANGER</b><span>21:00&ndash;03:00</span></div></div></div></section>

<section class="ck-s ck-lt"><div class="ck-w"><div class="ck-st"><span>04</span><h2>Guides</h2></div><div class="ck-gds"><a href="watch-setting-guide.html"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1793982141726-53a997414eed?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=400&q=75" alt="gold-tone watch with a textured olive dial" width="640" height="400" loading="lazy"><div><small>GUIDE_01 / 8 MIN</small><h3>The Watch Setting Guide</h3><p>Crown positions, safe date setting, hacking seconds and second time zones.</p></div></a><a href="watch-care-guide.html"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1792683422354-7a3779a6f1b8?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=400&q=75" alt="metal watch with a gold bezel on a wooden display" width="640" height="400" loading="lazy"><div><small>GUIDE_02 / 8 MIN</small><h3>The Watch Care Guide</h3><p>Winding, cleaning, magnetism, water and when to book a service.</p></div></a></div></div></section>

<section class="ck-s"><div class="ck-w ck-fq"><div class="ck-st"><span>05</span><h2>FAQ</h2></div><div class="ck-faq"><details open><summary>When is it unsafe to change the date on a watch?</summary><p>On many mechanical watches, avoid using the quick-set date between roughly 9 pm and 3 am, when the date-change mechanism is engaged. Move the hands to around 6 o&rsquo;clock first, then set the date.</p></details><details><summary>What is a GMT watch?</summary><p>A watch with an extra hand that goes around the dial once every 24 hours, usually read against a 24-hour bezel or scale. It lets you track a second time zone at a glance.</p></details><details><summary>How long will my automatic watch run off the wrist?</summary><p>That is its power reserve, often about 38 to 80 hours on modern movements. If you take it off on Friday evening, a 40-hour reserve may have stopped by Sunday morning.</p></details><details><summary>Can I wind an automatic watch by hand?</summary><p>Most can. Unscrew the crown if needed, then turn it gently clockwise 20 to 40 times to give a stopped watch a good start before wearing it.</p></details><details><summary>Should I set the time forwards or backwards?</summary><p>Forwards is the safer habit on most mechanical watches, especially near the date change. Some makers allow both directions; check the manual if you have it.</p></details><details><summary>How do I clean a metal bracelet?</summary><p>Soak it briefly in warm water with a drop of mild soap, scrub gently with a soft toothbrush, rinse and dry with a soft cloth. Only immerse the whole watch if its water resistance allows and the crown is closed.</p></details></div></div></section>

